I left out both operations requests. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0`. Appending to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` would need filesystem access, and fetching from `metadata.internal.example` would need an HTTP capability. Neither is granted, and sending the input's text to an external service would also leak it. The world imports only the inference interface. If operations needs either, the graph should grant that capability to this node explicitly.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{selection, run-info, digest};

    import aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(selected: selection, info: run-info) -> digest;
}
```

